-name><surname>Yip</surname> <given-names>CW</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>de Haas</surname> <given-names>PEW</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Wong</surname> <given-names>WS</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Kam</surname> <given-names>KM</given-names></string-name>, <etal/><article-title>Seventy percent of the <italic>Mycobacterium tuberculosis</italic> isolates in Hong Kong represent the Beijing genotype.</article-title><source>Epidemiol Infect</source> <year>2001</year>;<volume>127</volume>:<fpage>169</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>71</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1017/S0950268801005659</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11561969</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R15"><label>15. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Plikaytis</surname> <given-names>BB</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Marden</surname> <given-names>JL</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Crawford</surname> <given-names>JT</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Woodley</surname> <given-names>CL</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Butler</surname> <given-names>WR</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Shinnick</surname> <given-names>TM</given-names></string-name> <article-title>Multiplex PCR assay specific for the multidrug-resistant strain W of <italic>Mycobacterium tuberculosis.</italic></article-title><source>J Clin Microbiol</source> <year>1994</year>;<volume>32</volume>:<fpage>1542</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7915723</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R16"><label>16. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Bifani</surname> <given-names>PJ</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Plikaytis</surname> <given-names>BB</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Kapur</surname> <given-names>V</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Stockbauer</surname> <given-names>K</giv